{
  "id": "KS-HB-2016-2025",
  "scope": "state:ks",
  "title": "HB 2016 (2025-2026 biennium (2025 Regular Session)): HB 2016 Including funeral home online obituary notices as sufficient grounds for removal of a deceased voter from the voter registration books; requiring that poll workers be citizens of the United States and live within the state of Kansas; prohibiting the disqualification of active military members, spouses or other dependents who are citizens of the United States as poll workers on the basis of residency or being a registered voter; relating to advance voting ballot applications; modifying the requirements for soliciting registered voters to submit advance voting applications.",
  "urls": [
    "https://www.kslegislature.gov/b2025_26/bills/HB2016/",
    "https://www.kslegislature.gov/b2025_26/bills/download/?apn=b2025_26/year2/ready_for_publication/hb_2016/hb2016_enrolled.pdf",
    "https://www.kslegislature.gov/b2025_26/bills/download/?apn=b2025_26/year2/ready_for_publication/hb_2016/hb2016_00_0000.pdf",
    "https://www.kslegislature.gov/b2025_26/bills/download/?apn=b2025_26/year2/ready_for_publication/hb_2016/hb2016_01_0000.pdf",
    "https://www.kslegislature.gov/b2025_26/bills/download/?apn=b2025_26/year2/ready_for_publication/ccr_2025_hb2016_s_2167.pdf"
  ],
  "version": "enrolled",
  "operative_text": "(a_in_person_id)\n(section) K.S.A. 25-1122(b)\n(quote) (b) If the registered voter is applying for an advance voting ballot to be transmitted in person, the voter shall provide identification pursuant to K.S.A. 25-2908, and amendments thereto.\n(b_no_id_remedy)\n(section) K.S.A. 25-1122(d)\n(quote) (d) A voter may vote a provisional ballot according to K.S.A. 25- 409, and amendments thereto, if: (1) The voter is unable or refuses to provide current and valid identification; or\n(c_mail_ballot_id)\n(section) K.S.A. 25-1122(c)\n(quote) (c) If the registered voter is applying for an advance voting ballot to be transmitted by mail, the voter shall provide with the application for an advance voting ballot the voter's current and valid Kansas driver's license number, nondriver's identification card number or a photocopy of any other identification provided by K.S.A. 25-2908, and amendments thereto.\n(d_proof_of_citizenship) not stated.\n(e_other_rule)\n(section) Title: poll workers must be citizens and live in Kansas\n(quote) requiring that poll workers be citizens of the United States and live within the state of Kansas;\n(other) Funeral-home online obituary notices as grounds to remove deceased voters (K.S.A. 25-2316c); poll worker residency and military exception (25-2804); soliciting advance-voting applications (25-1122).\n(note) Off this topic: the bill sets no ID or citizenship-proof rule.",
  "sponsors": [
    {
      "name": "House Committee on Elections",
      "role": "prime",
      "version": "Enrolled (hb2016_enrolled); also read As Introduced (00), Senate Committee (01), Conference Committee Report (ccr_2025_hb2016_s_2167)"
    }
  ],
